leverage topology.

246
00:13:23,448 --> 00:13:26,286
Spreads across zones to give you higher,

247
00:13:26,286 --> 00:13:31,500
reliability and availability
and then monitor your pending pods.

248
00:13:31,929 --> 00:13:35,328
If that list starts getting really large,
you could have some other things

249
00:13:35,328 --> 00:13:37,077
that are going on.

250
00:13:37,077 --> 00:13:41,400
You can also combine these autoscaler
with a cluster autoscaler,

251
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:45,459
which can add or this scheduler
with the cluster autoscaler

252
00:13:45,591 --> 00:13:47,868
which can add additional nodes
to your cluster.

253
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:50,343
But be careful with that as well.

254
00:13:50,343 --> 00:13:54,336
If you're running in a cloud
and you've got a disaster that's happening

255
00:13:54,336 --> 00:13:58,230
and you tie it directly to your autoscaler
and it just keeps adding more and more

256
00:13:58,230 --> 00:14:02,025
nodes and you're consuming all the nodes
because something's out of control.

257
00:14:02,025 --> 00:14:06,777
You've got some funky while loop that's
spinning up pods and consuming resources.

258
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:10,308
You can blow through your,
cloud budget very quickly.

259
00:14:11,958 --> 00:14:13,179
All right.

260
00:14:13,179 --> 00:14:15,258
That's what a Kubernetes scheduler does.

261
00:14:15,258 --> 00:14:20,076
Matches pods to nodes efficiently,
sometimes very efficiently.

262
00:14:20,076 --> 00:14:21,264
If you have things wrong,

263
00:14:21,264 --> 00:14:24,927
it will do it very efficiently
and keep driving something wrong.

264
00:14:25,158 --> 00:14:27,798
Use filter
scores, affinities and priorities.

265
00:14:27,798 --> 00:14:32,649
When establishing your profiles and your
your pod requirements that you have.

266
00:14:33,012 --> 00:14:36,015
And remember,
the goal of this is high availability.

267
00:14:36,246 --> 00:14:41,064
Cluster efficiency,
which means grow and shrink, right?

268
00:14:41,163 --> 00:14:44,166
Don't
consume more resources than you need to.

269
00:14:44,265 --> 00:14:47,268
We kind of get lazy when we're running
in our own data centers,

270
00:14:47,499 --> 00:14:49,809
so be mindful of that
when you're running in the cloud,

271
00:14:49,809 --> 00:14:51,987
because those resources cost money.
